Make Codex reattachment lifecycle-safe

Use the existing Codex daemon endpoint before pod preparation.
Build frontend spawn parameters lazily from cached connection state,
and upload credentials only when no prior Codex state is known.

Keep frontends attachable even when repository configuration,
host credentials, or the host Codex binary are unavailable.

Serialize frontend proxy cleanup with cold creation, identify PTY
session generations, and discard stale pod connection state before
same-name recreation.
